[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"678","stub":{"id":"678","section":"Route 8A to Deerfield River","altname":"","river":"Chickley","difficulty":"IItoIII","states":["USA-MSS"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"3.86","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"levelFT","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"111910","location":{"latitude":"42.5890846252441","longitude":"-72.9379119873047"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117183","location":{"latitude":"42.6300773620605","longitude":"-72.902099609375"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"6","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[],"detail":{"id":"678","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"The gauge info has been taken from Cold Brook which is the neighboring drainage.\n\nNo additional information has been provided. If you know more about this run please leave a comment below.\n\nNew England Whitewater River Guide, Gabler R.\n\nTaken from a Trip Report by Bob Knapp:\n\nFlow was almost too low at 4.35, so it was a boney run. Yet it was a fun, technical, creeky run on a narrow river. Would like to run again at 5 feet or higher. Have to catch the river when it flashes after considerable rain or snow melt in spring. At 4.35 level, essentially a class II/II+ run, with one class III drop/slide called Lower Rapid. This rapid is about 0.5 miles below the Rt 8A bridge. In his book Classic Northeastern Whitewater Guide, Bruce Lessels states that *“the easiest run (for this rapid) is down the left side, but this one is a stern muncher whenever you run it unless the water is very high.”* We all ran different lines on this rapid with no significant issues.\n\nThere are 2 logs on this run that entirely block the river. Both are visible from the road, and they are at 1 mile and 2.6 miles from the turn on to Route 8 south. Both have a little water going over them but barely buffable.\n\n\\*\\*UPDATE THERE IS MORE WOOD IN RIVER VISIBLE FROM THE ROAD AS OF LATE MAY 2025\\*\\*\n\nTake-Out: we parked in Charlemont. To Put-In: go W from Charlemont for roughly 2.5 miles turning left on Tower Road, after 1.1 miles take at right onto Rt 8 A South, following the river upstream. We parked along the road at 4.0 miles from the Tower/Rt 8A intersection.","averageGradient":"25","maxGradient":"38","length":"4.9","correlations":[{"reachID":"678","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"levelFT","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"4.5","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"8"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"COLD RIVER AT FLORIDA, MA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01168250","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"10","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"3.86","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"42.66669444","longitude":"-73.0301667"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/01168250","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/01168250/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 4.5 - 8 levelFT  Comment: Estimated based on the Cold River\n\nMigration Errors: \nSingle range is valid but doesn't provide low/medium/high runnable\nThere is one comment for all of low/medium/high runnable.","comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"3.86","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30: